WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:27.910
In the Frame, by Polly Sweetman. It is the end of Lisa and Alice's holiday.

00:27.960 --> 00:31.150
They are leaving the Hotel Oracle.

00:31.200 --> 00:34.070
They are leaving Greece.

00:34.120 --> 00:36.870
They are going to the airport.

00:36.920 --> 00:41.230
They are going home.

00:41.280 --> 00:43.150
Goodbye, Kostas!

00:43.200 --> 00:45.110
Goodbye, Eleni!

00:45.160 --> 00:47.790
Thank you for our wonderful holiday!

00:47.840 --> 00:55.870
Come back to this island next year!

00:55.920 --> 00:59.630
Lisa and Alice are on the airport bus.

00:59.680 --> 01:03.790
The bus is stopping at another hotel.

01:03.840 --> 01:06.870
Some people are outside the hotel.

01:06.920 --> 01:13.470
They are going to the airport too.

01:13.520 --> 01:16.030
Look at that poor woman!

01:16.080 --> 01:19.350
She has two small children.

01:19.400 --> 01:22.150
She has a lot of luggage.

01:22.200 --> 01:24.430
And she has a pushchair.

01:24.480 --> 01:27.710
Let's help her.

01:27.760 --> 01:31.870
Lisa and Alice help the woman with her luggage.

01:31.920 --> 01:34.590
They help her with the pushchair.

01:34.640 --> 01:43.870
They help her with her children.

01:43.920 --> 01:48.390
I'm Lisa and this is my friend, Alice.

01:48.440 --> 01:50.110
Thank you, Lisa.

01:50.160 --> 01:51.750
Thank you, Alice.

01:51.800 --> 01:54.350
My name is Vera Brown.

01:54.400 --> 02:03.910
My children's names are Peter and Helen.

02:03.960 --> 02:06.310
I'm very worried.

02:06.360 --> 02:08.630
My husband is ill.

02:08.680 --> 02:10.630
He is in England.

02:10.680 --> 02:12.750
I must go to him.

02:12.800 --> 02:14.750
I'm going home.

02:14.800 --> 02:16.870
That's very sad news.

02:16.920 --> 02:19.630
I'm sorry, Vera.

02:19.680 --> 02:22.310
We're going to England too.

02:22.360 --> 02:25.630
We'll help you.

02:25.680 --> 02:28.870
Lisa and Alice are on the plane.

02:28.920 --> 02:31.630
Vera is on the plane too.

02:31.680 --> 02:35.270
She is sitting with her children.

02:35.320 --> 02:37.550
Look at this newspaper.

02:37.600 --> 02:40.790
Do you remember this painting?

02:40.840 --> 02:42.430
Yes.

02:42.480 --> 02:46.510
It's a painting from the island's museum!

02:46.560 --> 02:49.550
The artist is French.

02:49.600 --> 02:52.920
He's a famous French painter.

02:56.400 --> 03:01.470
The passengers are leaving the plane.

03:01.520 --> 03:04.510
Here we are in England, Vera.

03:04.560 --> 03:06.670
We'll help you at the airport.

03:06.720 --> 03:08.070
Thank you.

03:08.120 --> 03:12.030
You are very kind.

03:12.080 --> 03:16.550
Lisa, Alice and Vera are in the airport.

03:16.600 --> 03:19.840
Alice is getting their luggage.

03:23.320 --> 03:25.710
This is our last bag.

03:25.760 --> 03:28.270
Now we have everything.

03:28.320 --> 03:31.070
Now we must go to Customs.

03:31.120 --> 03:36.390
Please, I must go to the toilet!

03:36.440 --> 03:41.030
Vera is taking Peter to the toilet.

03:41.080 --> 03:42.670
Don't worry, Vera.

03:42.720 --> 03:44.470
I'll stay here.

03:44.520 --> 03:46.430
I'll stay with your luggage.

03:46.480 --> 03:49.310
Oh, thank you, Alice!

03:49.360 --> 03:53.670
Lisa, please go through Customs with Helen.

03:53.720 --> 03:56.350
Wait for Alice and me in the cafe.

03:56.400 --> 03:58.750
OK.

03:58.800 --> 04:01.150
Vera is at Customs.

04:01.200 --> 04:05.230
A customs officer is searching her luggage.

04:05.280 --> 04:09.110
Alice hears two customs officers talking.

04:09.160 --> 04:10.080
She is surprised.

04:14.040 --> 04:16.350
That is Vera Brownlow.

04:16.400 --> 04:18.310
She's an art thief!

04:18.360 --> 04:20.550
She steals paintings.

04:20.600 --> 04:22.030
Yes.

04:22.080 --> 04:25.870
But there are no paintings in her luggage.

04:25.920 --> 04:31.390
Oh! A painting is missing from the island's museum.

04:31.440 --> 04:34.110
And Vera is a thief!

04:34.160 --> 04:36.200
I must talk to these men.

04:43.480 --> 04:46.110
There's Alice!

04:46.160 --> 04:49.190
But where is Vera?

04:49.240 --> 04:51.870
Is she all right?

04:51.920 --> 04:53.200
Is Peter all right?

04:56.120 --> 04:58.870
Vera comes into the cafe.

04:58.920 --> 05:02.750
She is holding Peter's hand.

05:02.800 --> 05:04.630
Here we are at last!

05:04.680 --> 05:09.070
The customs officers are searching many travellers today.

05:09.120 --> 05:12.070
I'll take Helen and the pushchair now.

05:12.120 --> 05:14.430
My sister is going to meet me.

05:14.480 --> 05:18.230
She will help me with my luggage.

05:18.280 --> 05:20.830
Suddenly, there are customs officers

05:20.880 --> 05:24.270
and police officers in the cafe.

05:24.320 --> 05:27.990
One officer is searching the pushchair.

05:28.040 --> 05:30.950
He is looking in the frame.

05:31.000 --> 05:33.030
What is happening?

05:33.080 --> 05:36.790
Lisa, these are not Vera's children.

05:36.840 --> 05:39.550
They are her sister's children.

05:39.600 --> 05:42.710
Vera is an art thief.

05:42.760 --> 05:45.910
Do you remember the island's museum?

05:45.960 --> 05:49.310
Do you remember the stolen painting?

05:49.360 --> 05:53.560
The customs officers are looking for the stolen painting.

05:57.120 --> 06:01.310
The customs officers have the stolen painting.

06:01.360 --> 06:04.270
They are very pleased.

06:04.320 --> 06:07.190
Vera's sister has her children.

06:07.240 --> 06:10.190
She is very pleased, too.

06:10.240 --> 06:12.790
Well done, Lisa and Alice!

06:12.840 --> 06:15.710
There is a big reward for this painting.

06:15.760 --> 06:17.550
You'll get the money.

06:17.600 --> 06:19.390
That's great!

06:19.440 --> 06:23.030
We'll go on another holiday next year.

06:23.080 --> 06:24.560
LAUGHTER
